          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">10. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Most people searching for a "Yesoul treadmill review" have seen one of two machines: a folding
          treadmill with a big screen on top, at a price far below a Peloton or NordicTrack with a similar
          screen, or a new treadmill advertising a 30% incline and heart-rate-controlled Zone 2 training. Both
          are Yesoul’s, they are aimed at different buyers, and they come with quite different return and
          warranty terms. Independent hands-on reviews of either are still scarce, so this guide concentrates on
          what can be checked: the published figures, where they agree, and the terms you would be buying under.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. Is a Yesoul Treadmill Worth Buying? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A Yesoul treadmill is worth considering if what you want is a large screen at a modest price
            (the T3S Plus) or a full-size deck with an unusually steep incline (the T5 series), and you are
            comfortable buying a machine with little independent long-term coverage.</strong> The T3S Plus is a
            walking and jogging machine with a short belt and a one-year warranty. The T5 series is a different
            class of treadmill, with a 60-inch deck, a published continuous motor rating and a five-year frame
            warranty.
          </p>
          <p>
            Yesoul’s appeal is that it does not lock its screens behind a subscription. The T3S Plus mirrors your
            phone for free, and the T5 Max and Ultra run their own apps. That is a real difference from
            NordicTrack, ProForm and Peloton, whose screens are built around a paid membership, and it is why
            Yesoul turns up in searches for <a href="/best-peloton-alternatives/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Peloton alternatives</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            The caution is evidence. When we checked on 5 November 2026 we could find no full independent
            hands-on review of the T3S Plus or any T5 model from a major outlet; Consumer Reports lists the T3S
            Plus in its ratings, but behind a paywall. The T5 series only went on sale in the US in June 2026. That
            does not make the machines bad, but it means you are relying on Yesoul’s published figures and its
            trial period more than you would with an established treadmill brand. Buy where you can return it
            easily, and use the trial.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you only want the recommendation: the <a href="#yesoul-t3s-plus" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">T3S Plus</a>
            for walking and jogging with a big screen, the <a href="#yesoul-t5-plus" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">T5 Plus</a>
            for steep incline walking and running on a full deck, and the
            <a href="#yesoul-t5-max" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">T5 Max</a> only if you want the screen
            to run apps itself.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-yesoul-is" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. Who Yesoul Is, and Where It Sells</h2>
<p>
            Yesoul is best known for its exercise bikes, the G1M Plus and G1M Max among them, which pair a
            budget-to-mid-price frame with a large screen. Its US store also sells a rower, a <a href="/best-recumbent-bikes/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>recumbent bike</a>,
            treadmills and walking pads, accessories and multi-machine bundles. Yesoul’s US website does not say
            where the company is based or who owns it, and its footer gives only "Yesoul Fitness". Support runs
            through a help centre, a ticket form and email.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Where Yesoul treadmills are sold.</strong> Yesoul sells direct through its own US store,
            which offers free standard shipping on eligible orders. The T3S Plus also appears <a href="/best-buy-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>at Best Buy</a> and on
            Walmart’s marketplace. Amazon would not load for us on 5 November 2026, so we could not confirm which
            Yesoul treadmills it carries; the Amazon buttons on this page search for each model by name. Yesoul’s store also carries
            distributor listings marked "not for customer", including one for the T3S Plus at $1,199, which is the
            price retail partners are pointed to rather than a price you would pay.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Why the seller matters.</strong> Yesoul’s return policy, the 14 and 30-day home trials and
            the price-drop refund on the T5 apply to orders from Yesoul’s own store. A T3S Plus from Best Buy, or
            a Yesoul bought from any other retailer, follows that retailer’s return terms instead, which can be better or worse.
            Read our guide to <a href="/treadmill-return-policies/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill return policies</a>
            before deciding where to buy, and our guide to
            <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">buying a treadmill on Amazon</a>
            if a marketplace seller is involved.
